Subject: [PATCH 19/25] tei-v7 prompt-25: Contract-first issue decomposition

---
 config/livesweagent_swebench_pro.yaml | 2 +-
 tei/candidates.jsonl                  | 1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/config/livesweagent_swebench_pro.yaml b/config/livesweagent_swebench_pro.yaml
index d3b0158..c7d5d0b 100644
--- a/config/livesweagent_swebench_pro.yaml
+++ b/config/livesweagent_swebench_pro.yaml
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 agent:
   system_template: |
-    You are a helpful assistant that can interact multiple times with a computer shell to solve programming tasks. Work as a repository-aware maintainer: use the checkout's existing tooling, dependency constraints, test discovery rules, formatting conventions, and compatibility policy. Before reporting completion, confirm that the final diff is limited to the issue, that the selected checks actually exercise the changed path, and that no generated, unrelated, or environment-specific files were included.
+    You are a helpful assistant that can interact multiple times with a computer shell to solve programming tasks. Work as a repository-aware maintainer: use the checkout's existing tooling, dependency constraints, test discovery rules, formatting conventions, and compatibility policy. Before implementing, convert the issue into an explicit contract: identify the affected public behavior, the current behavior, the required behavior, invariants that must remain true, and the smallest set of code paths that can satisfy it. Trace each claim to repository code, tests, documentation, or the issue text rather than guessing. Then implement the narrowest coherent change. Before reporting completion, confirm that the final diff is limited to the issue, that the selected checks actually exercise the changed path, and that no generated, unrelated, or environment-specific files were included.
     Your response must contain exactly ONE bash code block with ONE command (or commands connected with && or ||).
 
     Include a THOUGHT section before your command where you explain your reasoning process.
diff --git a/tei/candidates.jsonl b/tei/candidates.jsonl
index 722834a..9b65435 100644
--- a/tei/candidates.jsonl
+++ b/tei/candidates.jsonl
@@ -51,3 +51,4 @@
 {"version_id": "prompt-21", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Repository-specific edge-case test matrix", "target_failure_mode": "Insufficient robustness across project-specific edge cases", "expected_dimension": "execution_accuracy", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-25102", "sympy__sympy-19783", "django__django-16569", "mwaskom__seaborn-3187", "sympy__sympy-15875", "sphinx-doc__sphinx-9602"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "config/livesweagent_swebench_pro.yaml", "find": "Treat this as a repository-specific maintenance task, not a generic coding exercise.", "replace": "Treat this as a repository-specific maintenance task, not a generic coding exercise. Before implementation, construct a compact test matrix covering the reported case, the normal legacy path, empty or missing values, singleton and boundary values, malformed inputs with the project's expected exception type, repeated or stateful use, ordering and mutation effects, and any alternate backend or compa"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.85, "reasoning_soundness": 0.87, "execution_accuracy": 0.85, "output_integrity": 0.89}, "aggregate": 0.865, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-25102", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-19783", "score": 0.94}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16569", "score": 0.93}, {"instance_id": "mwaskom__seaborn-3187", "score": 0.43}, {"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-15875", "score": 0.4}, {"instance_id": "sphinx-doc__sphinx-9602", "score": 0.41}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0175, "why": "The focused edge-case matrix is the strongest direct response to the weak probes and improves robustness across empty, singleton, boundary, and malformed inputs. It slightly reduces target alignment and output integrity because broad matrix construction can encourage scope expansion or brittle over-testing beyond the reported contract."}
 {"version_id": "prompt-22", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Behavioral compatibility and neighboring-pattern checkpoint", "target_failure_mode": "Insufficient robustness across project-specific edge cases", "expected_dimension": "reasoning_soundness", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-25102", "sympy__sympy-19783", "django__django-16569", "mwaskom__seaborn-3187", "sympy__sympy-15875", "sphinx-doc__sphinx-9602"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "config/livesweagent_swebench_pro.yaml", "find": "Before editing, identify the project's language and version constraints, test commands, module layout, public API conventions, and analogous fixes in history or neighboring code.", "replace": "Before editing, identify the project's language and version constraints, test commands, module layout, public API conventions, and analogous fixes in history or neighboring code. For each relevant neighboring implementation, compare input normalization, error handling, ordering, mutation, caching, and backend or version-specific behavior; follow the established convention unless the issue explicit"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.85, "reasoning_soundness": 0.83, "execution_accuracy": 0.77, "output_integrity": 0.89}, "aggregate": 0.835, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-25102", "score": 0.93}, {"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-19783", "score": 0.92}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16569", "score": 0.91}, {"instance_id": "mwaskom__seaborn-3187", "score": 0.31}, {"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-15875", "score": 0.27}, {"instance_id": "sphinx-doc__sphinx-9602", "score": 0.33}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": -0.0125, "why": "Neighboring-pattern comparison can catch compatibility and behavioral inconsistencies, but it risks importing assumptions from superficially similar code. That overgeneralization lowers alignment and execution accuracy, with little benefit on the hardest repository-specific probes."}
 {"version_id": "prompt-23", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Cross-repository reconnaissance before solution commitment", "target_failure_mode": "Uneven cross-repository generalization", "expected_dimension": "target_alignment", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-25102", "sympy__sympy-19783", "django__django-16569", "mwaskom__seaborn-3187", "sympy__sympy-15875", "sphinx-doc__sphinx-9602"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "config/livesweagent_swebench_pro.yaml", "find": "Consider the following PR description:", "replace": "Consider the following PR description. Before choosing an implementation, treat the repository as authoritative: locate the affected module, its public entry points, nearby tests, CI or supported-version configuration, and the project's documented behavior. Do not transfer assumptions, APIs, exception choices, or test commands from other repositories; derive them from this checkout."}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.91, "reasoning_soundness": 0.88, "execution_accuracy": 0.84, "output_integrity": 0.92}, "aggregate": 0.8875, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-25102", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-19783", "score": 0.94}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16569", "score": 0.94}, {"instance_id": "mwaskom__seaborn-3187", "score": 0.38}, {"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-15875", "score": 0.34}, {"instance_id": "sphinx-doc__sphinx-9602", "score": 0.39}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.04, "why": "Repository-authoritative reconnaissance improves cross-project transfer by grounding APIs, tests, CI, and documented behavior locally. It raises target alignment most, but reconnaissance alone does not guarantee a complete implementation and can consume effort without resolving subtle logic errors."}
+{"version_id": "prompt-24", "phase": "prompt", "technique": "Tooling- and compatibility-aware completion protocol", "target_failure_mode": "Uneven cross-repository generalization", "expected_dimension": "output_integrity", "evidence_instance_ids": ["scikit-learn__scikit-learn-25102", "sympy__sympy-19783", "django__django-16569", "mwaskom__seaborn-3187", "sympy__sympy-15875", "sphinx-doc__sphinx-9602"], "patch_or_prompt": {"file": "config/livesweagent_swebench_pro.yaml", "find": "You are a helpful assistant that can interact multiple times with a computer shell to solve programming tasks.", "replace": "You are a helpful assistant that can interact multiple times with a computer shell to solve programming tasks. Work as a repository-aware maintainer: use the checkout's existing tooling, dependency constraints, test discovery rules, formatting conventions, and compatibility policy. Before reporting completion, confirm that the final diff is limited to the issue, that the selected checks actually e"}, "dimensions": {"target_alignment": 0.89, "reasoning_soundness": 0.87, "execution_accuracy": 0.86, "output_integrity": 0.94}, "aggregate": 0.89, "probe_scores": [{"instance_id": "scikit-learn__scikit-learn-25102", "score": 0.96}, {"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-19783", "score": 0.95}, {"instance_id": "django__django-16569", "score": 0.94}, {"instance_id": "mwaskom__seaborn-3187", "score": 0.4}, {"instance_id": "sympy__sympy-15875", "score": 0.37}, {"instance_id": "sphinx-doc__sphinx-9602", "score": 0.42}], "score_label": "PROXY", "decision": "applied", "apply_note": "applied+committed", "delta_vs_baseline": 0.0425, "why": "The completion protocol improves practical execution by enforcing repository tooling, discovery, formatting, compatibility, and a disciplined final report. It provides the best output-integrity gain and a modest execution gain, but is broad enough that it adds less problem-specific reasoning than an invariant or edge-case-focused approach."}
